Z||000024||artherd||08-29-2001||01:47 AM||||Very Very Nice!  <P>I'd loose the ridges on the headlight doors, and it really looks like it could use a ~3" chassis streatch in the rear... (I've always thought this about fieros actually.)   It's very F50, and that is NOT a bad thing!!  I like the testarosa-esque slats, just make sure they're really elegantly formed and continue deep into the scoop.<P>trying to do a scoop will just look like a (very) poor 355 ripoff, that car just has *The Look* that can't be duplicated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Consider slight rounding to the angles in front, 355 style curves. I like the general shape though, definately a keeper.<P>Try it with a ~2-3" choped top, wicked-cool design!  (WAY better than that 'other' purple widebody, which I do like. But not like this, Aus is the MAN!)<P>Best!!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
